{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 0,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The president of the United States\nrecently shared this photoshopped"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3600,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "image on social media showing\nNATO leaders a map where the U.S."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7440,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has taken control of not only Venezuela,\nbut, more shockingly, territory"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12280,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from loyal NATO allies that helped the US\nfight several wars in the past decades."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17280,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Specifically, Denmark and Canada."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19840,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To many, this seems like something\nonly a madman would do."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23720,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But according to a viral speech\nby Canadian Prime Minister"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27080,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Mark Carney,\nthis is all part of a bigger trend."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30840,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is a return to an era\nof great power rivalry"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36080,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the rules based order is fading,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39000,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the strong can do what they can,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41320,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the weak must suffer what they must."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45120,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And while Carney\nhas a completely different"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47200,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "vision on how to behave\nin such a new world order."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50560,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The overall idea that we are moving back\nto an era of great power competition"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56360,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is actually in line with what\none of the architects of Trump's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59960,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "foreign policy, Stephen Miller,\nrecently told CNN's Jake Tapper."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65280,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But we live in a world in the real world,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68920,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Jake, that is governed by strength,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73040,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that is governed by force,\nthat is governed by power."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76680,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Therefore, it makes sense that Trump's new\nnational security strategy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80920,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "literally says they are returning\nto the so-called Monroe Doctrine,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85600,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "under which the US has historically sought\nto keep other"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89200,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "great powers\nout of the Western Hemisphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92280,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This means that, according to Miller,\nthe US will now be using its military"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97080,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to secure our interests\nunapologetically in our hemisphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101000,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's exactly what we've seen\nin the last few weeks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103880,
    "dDurationMs": 680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Isn't it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104560,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Therefore, some, like Doctor Wes Mitchell,\nhave said that Trump's actions are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109200,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in fact rooted in a clear\nand compelling logic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112600,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "grounded\nin the discipline of grand strategy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116000,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what is this logic?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117960,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, one word consolidation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120520,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Venezuela. Greenland. Canada."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122040,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The US is acting like a great power\nthat is consolidating its power"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126120,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in its own hemisphere\nto recover its strength first,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129720,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which will allow it to ultimately compete\nwith other great powers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132800,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like Russia and China\nin a new era of great power competition."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137000,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, according to the authors\nof a recent viral international relations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141320,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "paper, Professor Stacy\nGoddard and Abraham Newman,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144760,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this explanation does not make much sense\nbecause actually, upon closer inspection,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149840,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Russia's and China's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151160,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "activities in Venezuela and around\nGreenland are extremely limited."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155280,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On top of that, their resources are way\ntoo expensive to truly benefit the US."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160440,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Therefore, they argue\nthat to truly understand Trump's attacks"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163680,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on neighbors and allies, we need to view\nthe new international order"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167360,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through the lens of what came\nbefore the era of great power competition."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172040,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The era of competing royal houses\nthat cared about"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 175640,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "personal wealth and personal status."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178440,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To see how that works other than human."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181000,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know, I think Sisi and I always give\nthe example of, Game of Thrones."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185760,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know,\nit's like every almost everybody on earth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189320,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "relates to this show\nabout a small group of elites"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192920,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who really don't care\nabout their societies in general."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 196080,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They just care about redistributing\nresources amongst these houses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200040,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that is a system\nthat for most of, of human"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203560,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "history,\ndominated international relations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206960,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So could it be\nthat if we view Trump as a neo royalist"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210960,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the refinery and mineral mining owning\nbillionaires around him as his court,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215720,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Venezuela, Greenland,\nand also strangely high tariffs"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 219360,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "against China's biggest rival, India,\nit will all fall into place."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224120,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So who is right is the new world order\nwe are seeing right now a Trump versus"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228000,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ghani style\nreturn to great power politics, or rather,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231400,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the return of the corrupt politics\nof royal dynasties."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 234960,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To find out, I did, on the one hand,\na massive deep dive into the fundamentals"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 239400,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the history of great power politics\nand how it compares to Trump's new"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 243600,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "national security\nstrategy versus Ghani's speech."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246960,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And, on the other hand,\nan in-depth interview with Professors"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250240,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Godard and Newman."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252160,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But before we get into which story\ncan explain the New World order best,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 256800,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we need to understand what we are leaving\nbehind."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260200,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is the rise and fall of the rules\nbased liberal international order."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 265320,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Newfoundland, Canada, 1941."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 267520,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Churchill, arguably still the leader\nof the most powerful empire"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271200,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the world has ever seen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 272640,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meets his counterpart from the richest\nnation on Earth, Franklin D Roosevelt."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278000,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Together, they sit down to discuss what\nthey see as the ideal international order,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283040,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an order that would never again produce\nanother devastating world war."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287880,
    "dDurationMs": 400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And here"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 288280,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they've just agreed on the first pillar\nof the rules based international order,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 292320,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which means that nations have borders\nthat should be kept as they are."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296960,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They have a right to self-governance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 299280,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They have a right to trade freely,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 302200,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they can decide with whom they trade."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 305120,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And finally, the seas should be kept open\nto facilitate this international trade."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 310240,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, the second pillar\nof the liberal rules"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312840,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "based international order was economic."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315960,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And for that, we have to go back\nto Bretton Woods, the United States, 1944,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320680,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "44 nations come together\nto put an end to economic chaos."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 324840,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The economic case of the 1930s and 40s."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 327720,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This conference sets the stage for\nthe following international institutions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 331720,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that will create order."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 333320,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Where before there was chaos,\nthe General Agreement"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 336760,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on Tariffs and Trade that would later\nturn into the World Trade Organization."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 340920,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This meant that tariff\nshould be the same for everyone."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 344160,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then there's the world Bank."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 345240,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All poor countries should get loans\nto develop independent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 348360,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of their political allegiance\nto certain great powers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 352320,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then there's the IMF."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353440,
    "dDurationMs": 680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Getting loans"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 354120,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to save your currency from collapsing\nwill now depend on your economic program,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 358560,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rather than your political allegiance\nto certain great powers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363160,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Finally, the third pillar of the rules\nbased order"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 365840,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was the UN, a community of states,\nboth strong"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 368840,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and weak, that all pledged to follow\neven more rules."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 372800,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "1944 Dumbarton Oaks,\nthe United States 1945"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 377120,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yalta, the Soviet Union, and finally 1945\nSan Francisco, the United States."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 382600,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These conferences\nled to the creation of the United Nations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 386200,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Countries\nthat signed the UN charter agreed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389000,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that they would respect\nnumber one, human rights."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 392440,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Number two, international law."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 394800,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Number three, they signed that armed force\nshall not be used"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 398440,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "safe in the common interest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 400800,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then finally, that the goal\nof this new international order"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 404360,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was to promote the economic\nand social advancement of all people."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 408840,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Very lofty goals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 410040,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And just as with Bretton Woods,\nthis led to the creation of some"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 413280,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "international institutions\nwhich theoretically made it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 416960,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more difficult for states\nto act on their own in key areas like war,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 422080,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which was only allowed\nif the UN authorized it and justice states"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 427560,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were held accountable\nby the International Court of Justice."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 431800,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On top of that,\nsome states went even further"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 434600,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by signing up to the International\nCriminal Court, which could and did"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 439000,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sue leaders from weaker states\nlike Sudan and the Congo."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 443280,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But crucially, as Kony admitted,\nwe knew the story"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 447200,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the international rules\nbased order was partially false"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 451080,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the strongest would exempt themselves\nwhen convenient,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 454320,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that trade rules\nwere enforced asymmetrically."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 459840,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we knew that international law applied\nwith varying rigor"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 462680,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "depending on the identity of the accused\nor the victim."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 465960,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example,\nthe International Criminal Court"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 467760,
    "dDurationMs": 1240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has issued arrest warrants"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 469000,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "against Putin and Netanyahu,\nbut they are practically untouchable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 473000,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The IMF was far stricter, enforcing\npainful economic reforms on small powers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 478040,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like Egypt, Greece\nand Argentina than against"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 481240,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "strong countries like the UK."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 484240,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Also, the UN sanctioned small powers\nlike Zimbabwe and North Korea for human"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 488040,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rights abuses, but never strong countries\nlike China, the Soviet Union and the US."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 492680,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For similar offenses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 493880,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And despite countries\nsigning up not to invade one another"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 497200,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "except for self-defense,\nboth Western and Eastern powers invaded"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 500680,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "several countries during this so-called\nliberal rules based order."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504520,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Still,\nwe cannot be 100% sure that this was"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 507080,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because of the rules based order\nand international institutions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 510680,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in hindsight, I think we can say that\nthe liberal international order"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 515000,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "looked like a big success."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517280,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There were no new world wars, and even\nwithout taking those into account,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 520720,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the years from 45 to 2011 had relatively"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 523960,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fewer conflicts between states\nthan the decades before them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 527160,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We can also see that in the liberal order,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 529080,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "relations between countries on average\ngot much friendlier."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 532760,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We even saw several countries\njoining a security community in NATO."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 536800,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And on the flip side,\nwe saw far less countries being in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 539960,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "severe or lesser rivalry\nlike France, Germany, in the UK,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 544120,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which used to always\nbe at each other's throats."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 547520,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Finally, on the economic side,\nafter a massive reduction in global terms,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 551360,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we saw an explosion in global trade\nand more importantly,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 554760,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we saw a massive reduction\nin global poverty."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 557720,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And yet, while free trade under the rules\nbased international order"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 562200,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "arguably helped drag millions\nout of poverty, especially in Asia,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 566000,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the bottom 50% of Americans\nsaw their share of income drop"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 569800,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "remarkably, in the second half\nof the liberal rules based order."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 573960,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it is perhaps no wonder that Americans\nelected a candidate twice"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 578160,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that talked openly\nabout blowing up this liberal order."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 582000,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But we have to be honest, it was not\njust Trump that started this process."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 585360,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The three great powers actually seem\nto have been in on it together."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 590560,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, in 2014, member of the UN\nPermanent Security Council Russia"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 594720,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "annexed Crimea and then in 2022,\nseveral other provinces from Ukraine."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 600000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Next, when it comes to the economic\npillar, Trump's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 603000,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "2018 tariff barrage already\ncompletely undermined"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 606120,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the principle of low tariffs\nthat should be equal against all nations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 610160,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meanwhile, China\nactively undermined the IMF and world Bank"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 613800,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when it became one of the biggest lenders\nto poor and crisis stricken countries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 618760,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Finally, both China and Russia already\nhad a terrible human rights record,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 623160,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and honestly,\nthe US lost a lot of credibility in 2003."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 626880,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the Bush and Cheney,\nwhen they essentially authorized"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 629280,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the use of torture in CIA black sites\nand in Guantanamo Bay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 634200,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Still, Trump now almost announcing\nnew tariffs against a new nation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 638040,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every month and threatening to annex\nterritories from its most loyal allies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 642800,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That genuinely looks like the final nail\nin the coffin of the rules"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 646960,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "based international order."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 648880,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So no wonder that Carney said that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 651840,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we are in the midst of a rupture,\nnot a transition."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 655320,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The liberal, rules based\ninternational order is dead about that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 658400,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Almost everyone agrees."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 660160,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The real question is what's next?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 662160,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Are we heading back to an era\nof great power competition like Carney"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 665760,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the Trump\nadministration seem to believe?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 667720,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or should we think back"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 669280,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "further, that Trump's chaotic actions\nare better understood through the lens"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 673280,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the emergence of new kings\nand cohorts of billionaire backers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 677560,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "such as the Trump dynasty,\nthe House of Putin and the House of Modi?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 682000,
    "dDurationMs": 720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chapter two."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 682720,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What will the new global\norder actually look like?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 688240,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first\nview is that we are now heading back"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 690560,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to a new era of great power competition,\nwhere great power leaders like Trump"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 695600,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Putin have a very different vision\nthan middle power leaders like Ghani."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 701120,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This means that the world will look a lot\nmore like it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 703400,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "did in the 18th, 19th,\nand early 20th centuries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 707520,
    "dDurationMs": 840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "International relations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 708360,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Scholars tend to refer to this order\nas the Westphalian Global Order."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 712720,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After the Treaty of Westphalia in 1648,\nwhich greatly reduced the power"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 717200,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of royal houses in favor of nation states\nand their bureaucracies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 721520,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this new Westphalian order, you may say\ninternational institutions like the UN,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 726080,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "IMF and World Trade Organization lose\nwhat's left of their waning power."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 731160,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead, the world will once again\nbe completely determined by the actions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 734480,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of great powers like the US, China,\nRussia, and perhaps India and Europe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 739640,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "According to international relations\nprofessor John Mearsheimer,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 742920,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who famously belongs to the school of\nthought known as realism in such a world"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 748800,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "order that states can never be certain"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 751960,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that they won't end up living next door"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 755160,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to a really powerful state\nthat has malign intentions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 760240,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All of that causes states"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 763640,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to do everything they can\nto be as powerful as possible,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 768640,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and depending on how powerful they end up\nbeing, States are then classified"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 772840,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as great powers,\nmiddle powers, or small powers,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 775880,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they will all play\na different variation of the power game."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 780640,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First,\nsmall powers will either try to survive"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 783320,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by claiming neutrality, like Sweden\nand Belgium did in the Second World War,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 787440,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or by aligning themselves"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 788800,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with a great power for protection\nlike Finland and Hungary did."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 792960,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meanwhile, middle powers will either try\nto play great powers off against one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 796920,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "another like India has historically done,\nor they will do the same"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 801240,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that Ghani suggested in his speech,\nwhich is value based realism,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 806360,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "meaning that liberal countries\nlike Canada and Finland, for example,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 810640,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for every geopolitical situation\nthey will weigh their liberal values,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 814760,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "such as the importance of human rights,\nrespecting boundaries and democracy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 819480,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they will weigh that with geopolitical\nreality, especially for Canada."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 823760,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is a break with the past concretely,\nwhereas Canada's previous Prime minister,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 828360,
    "dDurationMs": 680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Justin Trudeau,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 829040,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "frequently challenged great powers\nlike China on their human rights records."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 833400,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ghani is subtly indicating\nthat Canada may no longer do this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 837240,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the geopolitical reality is\nthat this would get Canada"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 840200,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into trouble\nwith a great power simultaneously."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 843280,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Currently, in the case of the way forward,\nmaybe for a liberal value"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 846360,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "based mill powers to form coalitions\nwith countries"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 849360,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with similar values that may help them\nstand up to great powers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 853400,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with different values,\nsuch as Trump's America."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 857400,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You see, while the Trump team also rides\nin their national security strategy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 861240,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that they believe in realism, now\nthey give a version of it a different name"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 867520,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "flexible realism,\nwhich so far seems to mean might is right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 872000,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A strong country like the U.S."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 873440,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can take Greenland from Denmark,\nbecause Denmark is a tiny country"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 878520,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with a tiny economy and a tiny military,\nthey cannot defend Greenland."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 884320,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is what international scholars\nmean when they say might is right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 888080,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The US should get Greenland\nbecause it is strong enough to defend"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 891840,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Greenland from other great powers,\nand Denmark is not."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 895200,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But why does a great power like\nthe US need to do this in the first place?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 898960,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Aren't they already powerful enough?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 901320,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No. Say scholars like wertheimer,\nwithout international commitments"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 904840,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to respect borders."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 906920,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even great powers like the US, Russia\nor China will always fear that another"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 911160,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "great power will become much stronger\nthan them, upsetting the balance of power."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 916000,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Therefore, they may even want to dominate\nyour region of the world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 921240,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is because in that situation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 924680,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there is no other state\nthat is capable of hurting you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 929400,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this logic leads\nto so-called spheres of influence,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 932920,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where great powers\ntry to deny other great powers the ability"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 936720,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to threaten them\nby keeping them as far away as possible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 940920,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the 19th and 20th centuries,\nthe US tried to keep other great powers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 944400,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "out of the Americas under the so-called\nMonroe Doctrine and using similar logic."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 949280,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hitler at some point actually proposed\na sphere of influence in Europe,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 952520,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which he called the German\nMonroe Doctrine,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 955400,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and people like Professor\nMearsheimer have used this logic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 958720,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the Monroe Doctrine\nto make the case that the West provoked"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 961720,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Russia into invading Ukraine\nby meddling in its sphere of influence."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 966960,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Trump team has written\nin the national security strategy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 970200,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that they are essentially returning\nto the Monroe Doctrine."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 974600,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Some call it the donno\ndoctrine now, and some, like Doctor West"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 978480,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Mitchell, have used this type of logic\nto argue that term strategic actions are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 982760,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in fact rooted in a clear and compelling"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 984560,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "logic, firmly grounded\nin the discipline of grand strategy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 988400,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He says that Russia and China are the US\nnatural great power competitors,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 992720,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but that the US no longer has the strength\nto fight them all over the world,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 996880,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and therefore the US is now essentially\nretreating to its own Western Hemisphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1001280,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just this is done\nhistorically, many times before."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1004640,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Venezuela and Greenland are both\nabout securing access to vital resources"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1008760,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and, crucially,\nabout denying them to competitors."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1012600,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what we've seen so far is simply\na return to great power competition."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1016960,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Everything the US has done\nso far is just in the national interest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1021000,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Flexible realism is a cynical\nbut not illogical take on America First."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1026040,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, to me\nthere were at least three details"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1028640,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about recent events\nthat I could not explain with this theory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1032600,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, capturing Maduro\ndoes not seem to have been in US"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1036320,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "national interest,\ngiven that the oil there is too expensive"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1039120,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to get out of the ground,\nand China did not get that much anyway."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1043400,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Second, annexing Greenland\nand in the process completely alienating"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1047040,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "European allies does not make much sense\neither, given that the US already"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1051480,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "had almost unlimited"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1052760,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "military access to the island\nand easy economic access to its minerals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1057000,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Finally, if Trump was truly following\na great power style strategy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1060680,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "why did he recently tear of the hell\nout of India,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1063280,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is China's natural rival in Asia?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1066280,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is where Godard and Newman's\nneo royalist theory"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1069520,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "starts making a lot more sense."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1071720,
    "dDurationMs": 760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They claim that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1072480,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what we are seeing today is,\nrather than a system of territorial nation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1077200,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "states, rather than a system of rule\ngoverned institutions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1081880,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What we see\nis a system of international politics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1084680,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that structured\naround the interest of ruling clicks,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1088480,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which include a personalized,\nabsolute sovereign,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1091760,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and basically his network\nof whether or not his family,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1095360,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whether or not its financial interests,\nideologues that legitimate his rule."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1099640,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They call this neorealism\nbecause rather than a return to great"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1103240,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "power politics of the Westphalian order,\nit would potentially be more like a return"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1107480,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the world order\nbefore the Peace of Westphalia in 1648."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1112040,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You see, the Peace of Westphalia\ncame about to put an end to various"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1116160,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "devastating wars that plagued the Holy\nRoman Empire, Wars that often came about"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1121280,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because of royal succession,\nnot the national interest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1125320,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, the Dutch War of Independence\nagainst Spain arguably came about"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1129960,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "after that suddenly found themselves\nwith a new Spanish king that had"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1134120,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "essentially inherited the Netherlands\nthrough a series of marriages."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1139600,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in the royalist system,\nthe main actors were not states,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1143080,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but rather ruling monarchs\nand their clicks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1146360,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Therefore, most wars in those days were\nnot about the national interest at all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1150800,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They were about increasing royal wealth\nand status."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1155280,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Similarly, Godard and Newman argue\nthat in the case of Maduro's capture,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1159600,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Greenland and the tariffs against India,\nit's not about national interest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1164200,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's about this small group of hyper\nelites, these"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1167920,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this clique actor\nkind of clusters interest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1170840,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so that really drives\na very different logic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1173520,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of how international politics functions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1175440,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So while Venezuela's oil is too expensive\nto benefit the American oil industry"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1179120,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as a whole,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1180080,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the specific American refineries\nthat did benefit just so happened"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1184280,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to be controlled by Trump Mega-Donors,\nsuch as John Edison from Vidor."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1189120,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Similarly, while Greenland's\nminerals are not worth enough"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1192040,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the US to alienate\nallies over, that price"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1194800,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "may well be worth it to billionaires\nwith extensive interest in Greenland"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1199400,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like Ronald Lauder, who reportedly\nput the idea into Trump's head in 2018."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1204600,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Finally, there's Trump's\nmega tariffs against India."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1207560,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Again, from a great Barr perspective,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1209600,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it makes no sense to alienate\nChina's biggest Asian rival."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1213440,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if you consider that Modi\nvery publicly humiliated Trump by stating"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1217480,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that he had nothing to do with Pakistani\nIndian fees in the summer, Indian tariffs"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1221840,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "immediately after that incident start\nmaking a lot more sense."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1226320,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But while neorealism can fill\nin a lot of gaps"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1229800,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in their article,\nGoddard and Neumann do recognize that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1232600,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Royals dynamics\nhave always been in the background."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1236120,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After all, even during the height\nof great power politics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1238800,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the 19th century Belgian King Leopold,\nfor example, used the Belgian state"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1242960,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to conquer and dominate\nhis own personal colony in the Congo."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1247440,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And even today, Trump style\npersonal rule is quite common."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1251480,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, the difference between MBS\nor Orban and Trump is that they just don't"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1256640,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have the material or status capability\nto transform the international system."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1262040,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's why Trump is so exceptional,\nbecause he has the U.S."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1265720,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "military and the U.S. economy behind it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1267800,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In other words, just as Westphalian style,\ngreat power politics were always"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1271400,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "still there in the background\nduring, for example, the Cold War."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1274560,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Goddard and Neumann argue\nthat royalist elements are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1277640,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and have always been a part\nof the international order as well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1281880,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Therefore, my conclusion,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1285560,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "my conclusion\nis that to truly make sense of where"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1288440,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the global order is going,\nwe need all three lenses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1292240,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If going, you can make international\norganizations become more powerful again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1295800,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The global order will again\nbecome more predictable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1299040,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if they become weaker, we will either\nsee more great power games"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1303200,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where small and medium powers like\nUkraine, Venezuela and perhaps even Canada"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1307880,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "become pawns or battlefields\nfor great powers that continuously seek"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1312240,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to become more and more powerful\nbecause they fear that if they won't,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1316360,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they will not remain a great power\nfor very long."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1320000,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, if great powers are governed\nby autocratic or illiberal rulers,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1325520,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then we will increasingly see incidents\nlike Trump's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1328840,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Board of Peace, which he plans to stay on\neven if he is no longer U.S."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1332040,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "president, where great power influence\nwill not be used in the national interest,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1336920,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but rather to enrich Personalis leaders\nand their clicks or elevate their social"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1341800,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "standing amongst\na new class of global rulers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1345600,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and their courts that compete very much"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1348720,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like the royal houses of game of Thrones\nfor power and status."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1352640,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, given that Trump will be in power\nfor at least"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1355240,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "three more years, and given that far right\npopulist parties"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1358080,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are still lurking in the shadows\nin many other middle powers as well,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1361960,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think it's a safe\nbet that we will be seeing a more volatile"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1365720,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "international order emerging, which,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1367520,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whether it be for personal\nor national interest, tariffs, sanctions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1371360,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and even military strikes\nand wars, will sadly become more common."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1376000,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The economic evidence so far tells us that\nthis will make most of us"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1380120,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "poorer and less secure,\nespecially given that,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1383120,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "unlike in the 19th century,\ngreat powers now have weapons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1386960,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that could kill us all\nat the click of a button."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1389360,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Still, it doesn't have to be that way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1391560,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, some have argued\nthat at the Congress of Vienna"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1394880,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "after the body was defeated,\nthe return of realism looked inevitable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1398640,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yet this never happened."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1400560,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Similarly, who knows?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1401680,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Perhaps Trump's successor\nwill see the value of the liberal,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1404880,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
